  "id": "weak-central-coherence",
  "term": "weak central coherence",
  "definition": "Weak central coherence is a style of information processing in which a person focuses more on small details than on the overall meaning or whole pattern. In the supplied source, it is described in relation to autism spectrum disorder, where attention may be drawn more to parts of objects than to the object as a whole.",
